Linked code
-----------

The library statically links tract (https://github.com/sonos/tract), which is MIT OR Apache-2.0, and the crates it
depends on. Each of them is available under the MIT or the Apache-2.0 licence (some also under others, such as the
Unlicense), except foldhash, which is Zlib-licensed. The crates and their licences are listed by

  cargo tree -e normal --format '{p} {l}'

run in this directory. That list also shows the procedural macros (such as derive-new and zerocopy-derive) and what
they use (such as unicode-ident, which is also under Unicode-3.0); those run while the library is built and are not
linked into it. `cargo tree -e normal,no-proc-macro` lists only what is linked.

